 ## Overview
-A Monte Carlo estimator that samples volume boundary paths by first drawing the volume boundary vertex, then constructing two subpaths to connect it to the light source and the detector [S1][S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its parent, the [Unidirectional Volume Boundary Estimator](3538-unidirectional-volume-boundary-estimator.md), by decoupling the boundary integral from the interior term and building boundary light paths in a multi-directional manner to avoid costly silhouette edge searches [S2, unofficial]. Unlike the unidirectional approach which builds paths from the detector, this method samples the boundary vertex first, enabling a symmetric construction of source and detector subpaths [S1].
+A Monte Carlo estimator that samples volume boundary paths by first drawing the volume boundary vertex, then constructing two subpaths to connect it to the light source and the detector [S2][S3, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from its parent, the [Unidirectional Volume Boundary Estimator](3538-unidirectional-volume-boundary-estimator.md), by decoupling the boundary integral from the interior term and building boundary light paths in a multi-directional manner to avoid costly silhouette edge searches [S1][S3, unofficial]. Unlike the unidirectional approach which builds paths from the detector, this method samples the boundary vertex first, enabling a symmetric construction of source and detector subpaths [S1].
 
